USAGE -- what the undocumented programs say about themselves=============================================================334 programs on this disk have no documentation beyond their one line inDOC/INDEX.  The archive pool has a manual for 23 of them and no more; mostnever had one.  So each was asked `-?', the OS-9 convention, and what itsaid was kept.EVERY LINE BELOW CAME OUT OF THE PROGRAM.  Nothing here was composed.  Aprogram's own words about itself are worth more than prose written for itforty years later by somebody who never used it, and a captured line can bechecked by running the program again.`-?' is a convention, not a rule.  TeX prompts with `**' and reads standardinput, which is correct and is not a usage message.  Silence here is notevidence that a program is broken.    168   answered with a usage or syntax line    107   printed something else -- often the program simply running      9   faulted when given -?     50   said nothing at all--------------------------------------------------------------ANSWERED WITH A USAGE LINE -- 168--------------------------------------------------------------These told us how to invoke them.  The most useful thing on the page.  UnMacpack   (CMDS)      UnMacpack: unknown option -?      Usage: macunpack [-bsf3rduUailvqVH] [filename]      Use "macunpack -H" for help.  add_errmsg   (CMDS)      usage: add_errmsg "msg1" ... "msgN"      appends messages at the end of /dd/SYS/vi_errmsg      and reports seek positions  adlcomp   (CMDS/ADL)      Usage: adlcomp Infile (with any of the following)      -o Outfile              File for output      -i Dir                  Directory for INCLUDEs  adlrun   (CMDS/ADL)      Usage: adlrun [filename] [-d] [-h] [-r savefile]  adltouch   (CMDS/ADL)      Usage: adltouch <file> <number>  ape   (CMDS)      syntax: ape {opts}      Function: write gibberish in the style of <stdin> to <stdout>      Options:  aprocs   (CMDS)      Syntax: aprocs 